  "body": "Found while fixing #1635 (PR #1640). I read this from the code and have not reproduced it with a run.\n\n**What happens.** #1621 judges a part-source operation against the setup's OTHER parts (`keep_law::neighbour_parts`). It does so only for kinds that carry a part law, i.e. `depth_law_of(params, src, true)` is not `None`. A Drill with cross holes reads `DepthLaw::None`, so `neighbour_parts` is empty for it. Its chain answers only to `cross_part` against its own source's mesh, and since #1640 also against the setup's parts when the source is the stock.\n\nSo a cross hole drilled on part B, from a raw stock that also holds part A, whose drill or approach enters A, may carry no finding on the op. The program sim refuses to judge a posed (radial) chain, so whether such a program then posts is the open question.\n\n**Expected.** A part-source cross drill that enters a neighbouring part is a blocking finding on the op, or is refused by name.\n\nDone means:\n- a test with a part-source cross drill on B entering a neighbouring part A is refused or blocked;\n- the same drill clear of A still posts.\n\nPart of the #1621 / #1635 part laws.\n",
